### 1. Safe Statements to Publish (Verified & Tied to URLs)

* **"We use OpenAI and Anthropic APIs to generate draft responses. Neither provider uses customer API input data to train public or generalized AI models."**
* *Source:* [https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/10023548-how-long-do-you-store-my-data](https://privacy.claude.com/en/articles/10023548-how-long-do-you-store-my-data) & [https://openai.com/index/offering-zero-data-retention-for-frontier-models/](https://openai.com/index/offering-zero-data-retention-for-frontier-models/)


* **"API inputs and outputs are retained by our AI providers for up to 30 days solely for security monitoring and abuse prevention before being deleted."**
* *Source:* [https://explainx.ai/blog/anthropic-claude-30-day-data-retention-enterprise-zdr-august-2026](https://explainx.ai/blog/anthropic-claude-30-day-data-retention-enterprise-zdr-august-2026) & [https://meetily.ai/llm-privacy/openai](https://meetily.ai/llm-privacy/openai)


* **"Our cloud database and workflow software run on isolated DigitalOcean infrastructure, which encrypts data stored in databases using AES standards and protects communications via TLS encryption."**
* *Source:* [https://www.digitalocean.com/legal/data-processing-agreement-january-2026](https://www.digitalocean.com/legal/data-processing-agreement-january-2026)



### 2. Statements You Should NOT Publish

* **DO NOT publish:** *"Our AI providers immediately delete all review data as soon as a draft response is generated (Zero Data Retention)."*
* *Reason:* Unverified and false for standard API accounts. Both Anthropic and OpenAI maintain up to 30-day retention for abuse checks on standard self-serve accounts.



### 3. Account Tier Discrepancies (Self-Serve vs Enterprise)

* **Zero Data Retention (ZDR):** Standard self-serve API accounts **DO NOT** receive Zero Data Retention by default.
* OpenAI requires a custom ZDR application approval.
* Anthropic requires specific enterprise tier agreements and enforces 30-day retention across standard models.
